# Bracket and Ranking UI Rules

## Match Card Hierarchy

- Prioritize visual order: match stage/title > teams > score > metadata.
- Keep score as primary visual anchor (`font-extrabold`, larger size, `tabular-nums`).
- Metadata (time, court, match number) must remain compact and low emphasis.

## Winner/Loser Semantics

- Winner row must use explicit semantic styling (`emerald` accent, stronger border/background, winner badge).
- Non-winner row should be visually de-emphasized (`opacity`/neutral background) without losing readability.
- Do not rely on color alone; include text labels such as `VENCEDOR` or `CAMPEAO`.

## Final Stage Emphasis

- Final card must be more prominent than all other cards (strong gradient, ring, glow/shadow).
- Third-place card should be highlighted, but always below final in hierarchy.
- In-progress matches should have a clear live state (pulse/shimmer-like feedback), not subtle color-only changes.

## Athlete Avatar Cluster

- Team presentation should use dual-athlete avatar cluster when data exists.
- Each avatar must support:
  - image when `profilePhotoUrl` exists;
  - initials fallback when image is missing.
- Keep overlap, border, and size consistent across bracket and ranking screens.

## Category Finalization Ordering

- When category is finalized, display sections in this order:
  1) Final
  2) Third place
  3) Elimination rounds (semis/quarters/etc.)
  4) Group stage
- Finalized category screens should be result-first and read-only oriented.
